      "section": "shared.article-body",
      "variant": "plain",
      "content": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "This month we shipped changes that help climate teams turn one-off reporting projects into steady, repeatable programmes. The post covers what changed in how companies collect data, review it and share it, and what we expect to matter next."
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Everything here is illustrative placeholder writing for a fictional company. The structure, not the figures, is what this example demonstrates."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading-2",
            "text": "Data collection moved earlier"
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Most teams now request supplier data quarterly instead of once a year. Short templates, a named contact and a clear deadline made responses faster and far easier to compare. Read our [supplier engagement guide](/guides/mastering-scope-3) for a step-by-step approach."
          },
          {
            "kind": "bullet-list",
            "items": [
              "Quarterly requests replaced annual surveys",
              "Templates cut back-and-forth with suppliers",
              "Automatic checks flag gaps before review"
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "callout",
            "paragraphs": [
              "**Tip:** start with the suppliers that contribute the most to your footprint, then widen the request once the first cycle is complete."
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading-2",
            "text": "Review became a shared habit"
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading-3",
            "text": "Finance and climate teams worked together"
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Shared workspaces let finance reviewers see the same numbers as the climate team, with comments and history attached to each figure. Sign-off became a routine step rather than a scramble at the end of the cycle."
          },
          {
            "kind": "quote",
            "paragraphs": [
              "The best reporting season we have had was the one where nobody had to chase a spreadsheet."
            ],
            "attribution": "Placeholder customer, sustainability lead"
          },
          {
            "kind": "figure",
            "size": "m",
            "aspect": "4:3",
            "caption": "Illustrative review cycle, year over year",
            "image": {
              "assetRole": "artboard.diagram",
              "tone": "neutral",
              "alt": "Simple line chart of review time falling over four quarters"
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading-2",
            "text": "What to watch next"
          },
          {
            "kind": "table",
            "head": [
              "Area",
              "Today",
              "Next"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Supplier data",
                "Quarterly requests",
                "Continuous feeds"
              ],
              [
                "Review",
                "Shared workspaces",
                "Automated first drafts"
              ],
              [
                "Reporting",
                "Several frameworks",
                "One shared dataset"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "If you are planning your next cycle, the most useful step is to agree who owns each dataset and by when it is due. The tooling matters less than the habit."
          }
        ],
